            "review_title": "Review at Jaspas",
            "review_text": "Leean W\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam206 contributions\n0\nGreat Sunday Roast at Jaspas D2\nJun 2019 • Friends\nJaspas D2 is a very beautiful venue which has a great atmosphere on weekends and very friendly staff. I was delighted to see Vindaloo curry on the menu although it was only a bit spicy when it came. Despite this it was still a very pleasant meal with welcome accompaniments attractively presented. I would also have loved my goat's cheese to be warm served in breadcrumbs, rather than cold, in the goat's cheese salad but I recognise that this is just a personaI preference. Also, I hadn't been to Ho Chi Minh for a number of years so went for their tenderloin steak, on another visit, which used to be one of the best steaks in Ho Cho Minh. However I was a bit disappointed to discover that their tenderloin has been taken off their menu and so I settled for a different steak instead, I think it was the rump, There was quite a bit of fat, but easily removed and the pepper sauce was just as delicious, as always, as were the fat chip and buttery peas. But where Jaspa's really excels to my mind, is in their Sunday roast and delicious desserts. I hadn't really expected their roast to be so tasty to be honest as I usually go to a rival restaurant which makes fantastic Sunday roasts but in fact, unbelievably, Jaspas roast was even more delicious than the one we normally eulogize about! The staff were very helpful as it was a lamb roast that day and I asked if I could change to chicken, not being at all fond of lamb. This was pleasantly agreed to and the lunch was superb. The chicken was melt in the mouth, the mashed potato buttery and the variety of vegetables was broad and crisp. The roast potatoes were crispy and the gravy was super tasty. The rival restaurant also used to have the same quality roast but now they no longer add butter to their mashed potatoes and their roast potatoes are too soft so Jaspas is definitely coming out top for me. The lemon pie was gorgeous - sweet pastry and sharp lemon flavour balance beautifully and all of us agree that their banoffee cake is the best dessert tasted not just in Vietnam but anywhere, ever !!! Please Japas just bring back your tenderloin steaks and give a warm goat's cheese option and we'll love you forever! My 4 star rating for all of the dishes would definitely zoon up then from a 4 star to 5 star rating.....it is so close already.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 11, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
